automotive-wire-harness-tape-selection-guide.html:20:  <section class="page-hero dark-section"><p class="kicker">Procurement & engineering guide</p><h1>How to select automotive wire harness protection materials.</h1><p>Start with the application environment, then compare noise, abrasion, temperature, installation and harness-fixing requirements. This guide helps purchasing and engineering teams prepare a focused first technical enquiry.</p><div class="crumbs"><a href="index.html">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="products.html">Products</a><span>/</span><b>Selection guide</b></div></section>
automotive-wire-harness-tape-selection-guide.html-21-  <section class="inner-section light-section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="kicker">Step 1 / Define the application</p><h2>What does the harness need to withstand?</h2></div></div><div class="trust-grid"><article class="trust-card"><small>Interior routing</small><h3>Noise and movement</h3><p>For interior areas where squeak and rattle matter, identify the contact surfaces, motion points and target noise-damping requirement.</p><a class="text-link" href="automotive-fleece-tape.html">Explore PET fleece tape <span>↗</span></a></article><article class="trust-card"><small>Body and general harness</small><h3>Balanced abrasion protection</h3><p>For general routing, record the expected abrasion exposure, bend radius and operating temperature before selecting a fabric tape.</p><a class="text-link" href="polyester-fabric-tape.html">Explore polyester fabric tape <span>↗</span></a></article><article class="trust-card"><small>General bundling</small><h3>Flexibility and identification</h3><p>For flexible bundling or color identification, confirm flame-retardancy, low-VOC expectations, width and required color.</p><a class="text-link" href="pvc-wire-harness-tape.html">Explore PVC harness tape <span>↗</span></a></article><article class="trust-card"><small>Engine compartment</small><h3>Heat and shielding</h3><p>For high-temperature routes, document the maximum exposure, radiant heat and any shielding requirement before reviewing foil-based solutions.</p><a class="text-link" href="aluminum-foil-fiberglass-tape.html">Explore thermal shielding tape <span>↗</span></a></article></div></section>
automotive-wire-harness-tape-selection-guide.html-22-  <section class="inner-section dark-section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="kicker">Step 2 / Build a clear enquiry</p><h2>Six details that speed up the first technical review.</h2></div></div><div class="perf-grid"><article class="perf-card"><small>01</small><h3>Harness location</h3><p>Interior, body, door, roof, engine compartment, battery or another application area.</p></article><article class="perf-card"><small>02</small><h3>Operating conditions</h3><p>Expected temperature, moisture, fluid exposure, vibration and service environment.</p></article><article class="perf-card"><small>03</small><h3>Protection target</h3><p>Noise reduction, abrasion resistance, flexible bundling, thermal shielding or electrical insulation.</p></article><article class="perf-card"><small>04</small><h3>Supply specification</h3><p>Current material, width, roll length, color, packaging and estimated annual demand.</p></article></div></section>
automotive-wire-harness-tape-selection-guide.html-23-  <section class="inner-section light-section"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="kicker">Step 3 / Complete the protection system</p><h2>Tape is only one part of harness protection.</h2></div></div><div class="trust-grid"><article class="trust-card"><small>Cable management</small><h3>Protective sleeving</h3><p>Consider braided or self-wrap sleeving where installation access, cable breakout or stronger abrasion protection is required.</p><a class="text-link" href="expandable-braided-sleeving.html">Explore protective sleeving <span>↗</span></a></article><article class="trust-card"><small>Harness fixing</small><h3>Clips and cable ties</h3><p>For routing and retention, record mounting method, substrate, bundle diameter and the required temperature range.</p><a class="text-link" href="automotive-cable-clips-ties.html">Explore cable clips and ties <span>↗</span></a></article><article class="trust-card"><small>Manufacturing confidence</small><h3>Process visibility</h3><p>Review coating, rewinding, precision slitting and inspection capability when you assess a material supplier for a program.</p><a class="text-link" href="manufacturing.html">View manufacturing capability <span>↗</span></a></article><article class="trust-card"><small>Documented systems</small><h3>Quality documentation</h3><p>Confirm the applicable technical documentation and quality-system information for your supplier review process.</p><a class="text-link" href="quality.html">View quality information <span>↗</span></a></article></div></section>
